  "text": "SENATE•\nTHE PARLIAMENT OF THE COMMONWEALTH.\nRK/WH.\nCOMMONWEALTH PARLIAMENT OFFICES,\nBrisbane, B.9, Q'ld.\n25th October, 1957.\nDear Mr. McFadyen,\nAs I understand you will be\nleaving the Service shortly, may I wish you\ngood health\nand happiness in your retirement.\nIt is regrettable that it has\nnot been possible\nto\nbring down the\nnumerous\namenaments to the Navigation Act which are\ntrain, but I feel\nsure\nin\nthat such a consolidation\nmust always remain as a reminder of your service.\nKind regards,\nYours sincerely,\nClaude:\n(ROY KENDALL)\nSenator.\nC. H. McFadyen, Esq., C. B.E.,\nDepartment of Shipping & Transport,\nMELBOURNE, Vic.\nMARIE ANG TAYIR (5 MONTHS) FOREST HILL NEWTORI",
